import{_ as o,o as r,c as i,a5 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CsGesDJn.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"LTX director worker","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"feature/ltx-director-worker/spec.md","filePath":"feature/ltx-director-worker/spec.md"}'),t={name:"feature/ltx-director-worker/spec.md"};function d(n,e,s,c,l,p){return r(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="ltx-director-worker" tabindex="-1">LTX director worker <a class="header-anchor" href="#ltx-director-worker" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;LTX director worker&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Continue the approved Claude design: a 20-second product film, with <code>review</code> when a character image is supplied and <code>cinematic</code> otherwise. Claude on the application backend writes a validated director script. Qwen builds K0–K3; LTX renders two connected parts; VieNeu mixes optional narration and music.</p><h2 id="acceptance" tabindex="-1">Acceptance <a class="header-anchor" href="#acceptance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Acceptance&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Preserve Tuấn&#39;s architecture: backend-only <code>X-API-Key</code>, multipart submit, <code>prompt_id</code>, job polling, S3 output or authenticated media download.</li><li>Keep existing motion-reference and 5/10/15-second image video routes intact. Select LTX for 20-second image jobs only when LTX is configured.</li><li>Optional character image travels through the existing web and Business request into AI; no raw workflow or secret is accepted from the browser.</li><li>Validate the director schema and selected mode before ComfyUI submission. Override upload filenames and output prefixes server-side.</li><li>Convert generated GUI subgraphs into executable API nodes using the running server&#39;s node schema; reject unsupported serialization rather than submitting a guessed graph.</li><li>Deployment ZIP includes everything required to build the graph; installation preserves model files and running ComfyUI.</li><li>UI: optional character upload uses parallel Vietnamese/English keys and existing light/dark theme components. Character image means review; otherwise cinematic.</li><li>Invalid key, missing character, malformed script and unavailable ComfyUI return bounded actionable errors; failed generation retains existing credit handling.</li></ul><h2 id="verification-boundary" tabindex="-1">Verification boundary <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification-boundary" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification boundary&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Use mocked Claude/ComfyUI and real generated graphs locally. A live GPU render and listening to a selected voice remain hardware acceptance checks; do not claim them from mocked tests.</p><h2 id="revision-2026-11-18-wan-vace-worker-replaces-ltx" tabindex="-1">Revision 2026-11-18: Wan VACE worker replaces LTX <a class="header-anchor" href="#revision-2026-11-18-wan-vace-worker-replaces-ltx" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Revision 2026-11-18: Wan VACE worker replaces LTX&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The VM now runs Wan 2.2 Fun VACE (<code>wan_vace_bundle</code>) instead of LTX. Same transport (<code>LTX_WORKER_URL</code>/<code>LTX_WORKER_API_KEY</code>, <code>X-API-Key</code>, <code>script_json</code> + <code>reference_image</code>, <code>prompt_id</code>, job polling, <code>/api/v1/media</code>). Only the director script changes.</p><ul><li>Claude writes a VACE script, the same format as the 13 hand-made flows in <code>ltx-video/flows/&lt;genre&gt;/</code>: <code>genre</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>product_name</code>, <code>story</code>, <code>views</code> (4-side turnaround), one 2x2 <code>storyboard_prompt</code> (or two <code>storyboard_prompts</code> for cut films) and 3-7 <code>segments</code> (<code>prompt</code>, <code>start</code>, <code>end_panel</code>, <code>frames</code>).</li><li>Genre follows the brief: unbox, hero, tvc, lifestyle, asmr, before_after, food, tech, compare, fashion, home. Prompts follow <code>PROMPT_RULES_WAN.md</code> (anti-plastic checklist, ABCD for TVC).</li><li>Video is silent (VACE has no audio): no voice-over or music fields. Sound is added at editing.</li><li>An optional character image is sent as <code>extra_images</code> (storyboard image 3, after the product photo and the turnaround). No mode switch.</li><li>Size comes from the request aspect ratio (9:16 = 576x1024, 16:9 = 1024x576), never from Claude. Upload names and output prefixes stay server-side.</li><li>Validation before submission: schema, segment 1 not <code>prev</code>, panel numbers within the grids, <code>frames</code> 4n+1 in 17..85, total 15-21 s at 16 fps. Failure: no GPU job, no credit change beyond existing handling.</li></ul><p>Out of scope: S2V UGC talking flow through the API, web/Business changes, voice/music.</p><h2 id="revision-2026-11-18-b-product-video-page-uses-vace-instead-of-veo" tabindex="-1">Revision 2026-11-18 (b): Product Video page uses VACE instead of Veo <a class="header-anchor" href="#revision-2026-11-18-b-product-video-page-uses-vace-instead-of-veo" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Revision 2026-11-18 (b): Product Video page uses VACE instead of Veo&quot;">​</a></h2><p>User decision (option A): <code>/workspaces/:id/product-video</code> becomes the VACE 20 s flow. The scene-by-scene Veo pipeline (plan, storyboard review, per-scene quotes and retries, ffmpeg render) is no longer shown on this page; its code stays in the repo for rollback.</p><ul><li>Form: product photo (required, JPEG/PNG/WebP, max 10 MB), optional person photo (same limits), brief (required, max 1000 characters, the AI service legacy prompt limit), aspect ratio 9:16 (default) or 16:9.</li><li>Submit: existing <code>aiVideoService.generate</code> → Business <code>POST /workspaces/{id}/ai/videos</code> with <code>durationSeconds: 20</code>, <code>referenceImageBase64</code>, optional <code>characterImageBase64</code>. Credits: the existing <code>VIDEO_GENERATE</code> operation (refund on failure as today). No Business change.</li><li>Progress: existing background task dock (poll every 5 s); the page shows rendering state, then the MP4 player and a download link. A failed job shows the credit-aware error message.</li><li>UI states: idle, submitting, rendering (10-20 min note), completed, failed. i18n keys under <code>productVideo.vace.*</code> in both <code>vi/productVideo.json</code> and <code>en/productVideo.json</code>; theme tokens only (<code>bg-card</code>, <code>border-border</code>, <code>text-muted-foreground</code>, <code>text-brand-orange</code>), so light and dark both work.</li><li>Out of scope: storyboard preview before rendering, per-scene retry, recent-jobs list on this page.</li></ul><h2 id="revision-2026-11-18-c-photo-brief-only" tabindex="-1">Revision 2026-11-18 (c): photo + brief only <a class="header-anchor" href="#revision-2026-11-18-c-photo-brief-only" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Revision 2026-11-18 (c): photo + brief only&quot;">​</a></h2><p>User decision: the page asks only for the product photo and the brief. Claude decides genre, story, people and <code>aspect_ratio</code> (new required script field; the worker size follows it, the request aspect is ignored on this route). The person-photo and aspect inputs are removed from the page; the backend still accepts <code>character_image_base64</code>.</p><h2 id="revision-2026-11-18-d-background-music" tabindex="-1">Revision 2026-11-18 (d): background music <a class="header-anchor" href="#revision-2026-11-18-d-background-music" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Revision 2026-11-18 (d): background music&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The director picks one of the 5 bundled CC0 tracks (<code>resources/product-video/music</code>) in the required <code>music</code> field. After the worker MP4 is downloaded, the AI service loops/trims it to the video length with a 0.5 s fade in and 1.5 s fade out (ffmpeg, video stream copied, about 1 s). A mixing failure logs and delivers the silent video. No extra Claude call.</p><h2 id="revision-2026-11-19-e-veo-form-removed" tabindex="-1">Revision 2026-11-19 (e): Veo form removed <a class="header-anchor" href="#revision-2026-11-19-e-veo-form-removed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Revision 2026-11-19 (e): Veo form removed&quot;">​</a></h2><p>User decision: the product-video page shows only the VACE form. The Veo scene components, hook, service, types and their unit/e2e tests are deleted from <code>brandhub-web</code> (git history keeps them); <code>?productionId=</code> links now open the VACE form. Work restored from stash <code>wip-ltx-product-video-before-develop-20261118</code> onto new branch <code>feature/vace-product-video</code> in <code>brandhub-ai-service</code> and <code>brandhub-web</code>.</p>',19)])])}const m=o(t,[["render",d]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
